  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5a8b32bb-a3f8-46ef-b0d0-dd75eb5e4ae1.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 163px;\" /></p><p>The electron in the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mrow><mi>th</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math> orbit of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Li</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp; is excited to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> orbit using the radiation of energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>47</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> (as shown in the diagram). The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> is ___________</p><p>Given :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The difference energy between two energy levels is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>47</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>)</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>749</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the transition is taking place between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow></mrow></mover><mn>2</mn></math>, and it comes under Lymann series.</p><p>If we take&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>749</mn><mo>&#8771;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
